paper:
  title: "A Living Research Record: Version-Controlled Experiment Trees with Frozen Nodes"
  subtitle: "Every experiment is a node; the paper is the projection"
  version: "1.0"
  abstract: "We demonstrate a research-log discipline in which every experiment is a node in a durable, version-controlled tree. Nodes move from provisional to frozen (preregistered, immutable) to answered (terminal, carrying an outcome). Answered nodes form the results table, frozen nodes the in-progress register, and dead ends the discussion of negative results. All manuscript numbers are generated from the tree state and never hand-typed."

